{
  "purpose": "every hyperbolic SID metric the rounds proposed, what it measured on the confirmed pairs, and what it refuted; the next round's prompt carries the refuted list",
  "families": {
    "partition_geometry": "the table's own geometry: tightness, margin, dispersion, coverage, reach, ranking of cells -- measured, and none of it tracks the recall",
    "rewarding_an_answer_in_hand": "metrics that grow when the answer is already inside the cell: the path likelihood, the generator-side hit rate -- they are NEGATIVELY correlated",
    "behaviour_contrast": "the family that works: the table is contrasted against the behaviour reference with explicit positives and negatives, on the level-1 prefix centroid",
    "structural_alignment": "label-free structure comparisons: does the hyperbolic shared depth of a pair agree with the length of their shared SID prefix, does the prefix tree preserve the reference's distances, is a cell's angular cone tighter than a different set of the same size -- measured with the corrected definitions, and none of them is eligible",
    "behaviour_reference_obligation": "the table is scored against a CURVATURE, not against positives and negatives: the training behaviour fixes a reference graph, the four-point tree-likeness of that graph fixes the curvature, and the SID's own four-point deviation at that curvature is the metric. Measured on the 107 confirmed pairs it is the second strongest construction (rho +0.6605) and the curvature it estimates beats both a near-flat and a Euclidean control by +0.128 / +0.157 in a paired bootstrap. NOT refuted: the earlier rejection of the delta family was an artefact of six implementation defects, recorded in DELTA_SVD_PROTOCOL.md (v1 to v4).",
    "hyperbolic_properties_of_the_sid_table": "the other hyperbolic properties as SID-quality metrics: the Gromov product, radial depth, radial purity, geodesic slack, the entailment cone, angular branch separation, Busemann consistency, volume growth -- and the behaviour-aware versions of the geodesic and the Busemann. Each is measured with a Euclidean control and a PERMUTED control (the SID rows shuffled across the items). Measured on the 107 confirmed pairs: no family beats its permuted control, three are degenerate on the frozen reference (a thin shell at radius 0.9115 +- 0.0139, so radial depth, cones and volume growth are constant), and the behaviour-aware geodesic, once the ancestor depth is held fixed, is at chance. REFUTED as predictors: see HYPERBOLIC_FAMILIES.md."
  },
