      "metric_id": "lorentz_pmi_l1",
      "title": "Lorentz-hyperboloid posterior-mass lift of the level-1 cell above its training prior (a curvature-exact PMI between the frozen reference and the code).",
      "round": "round_20261030_033031",
      "proposed_by": "metric_ideation_4",
      "formula": "Setup. Items i = 1..N (N = 24587). The table gives level-1 code c1(i) in {1..K}, K <= 256. The frozen Issue #126 reference gives one Euclidean per-item representation x_i in R^d (its source side) and one frozen scalar temperature tau > 0. Fix curvature kappa = 1; nothing is fitted.\n  (1) Map.  y_i = tanh(tau*||x_i||) * x_i/||x_i||  (the exp map exp_0(tau x_i) of the unit Poincare ball; y_i = 0 if ||x_i|| = 0).  Lift to the Lorentz hyperboloid:  p_i = ( (1+||y_i||^2)/(1-||y_i||^2) , 2*y_i/(1-||y_i||^2) )  in R^{d+1}.\n  (2) Metric.  <a,b>_L = -a_0*b_0 + sum_{k=1..d} a_k*b_k  (Minkowski form, sig",
      "measured": false,
      "measurement": null,
      "family": "behaviour_contrast"
    },
    {
      "metric_id": "horo_cell_rank",
      "title": "Busemann (horospherical) height of each level-1 cell under the item's full training predecessor history, converted to a full-negative-population soft expected rank",
      "round": "round_20261030_040711",
      "proposed_by": "metric_ideation_2",
      "formula": "Notation. B^d is the Poincare ball of radius 1, curvature K = -1 (so c = 1); exp_x and log_x are its exponential and logarithm maps. N = 24587 items. code1(i) in {0..255} is the level-1 integer of item i in the exported SID table. s_i, t_i in B^d are the frozen Issue #126 reference's source and target representations of item i (learned on training pairs only). sigma(u) = 1/(1+e^{-u}). D_train is the training split of (history, target) pairs.\n1. Predecessor history of an item (whole training history, not one pair):\n   Pred(i) = the multiset union of the items j appearing in the histories of ALL",
      "measured": false,
      "measurement": null,
      "family": "behaviour_contrast"
    },
    {
      "metric_id": "hfsc_rank_l1",
      "title": "Hyperbolic free-energy cell rank \u2014 the chance-corrected soft rank of the true level-1 cell under a leave-one-out Karcher barycentre of the full training history, scored against the whole per-cell negative distribution.",
      "round": "round_20261030_040711",
      "proposed_by": "metric_ideation_3",
      "formula": "Work in the open ball B^d = {x in R^d : ||x|| < 1} at constant curvature c = -1, with the Poincare Riemannian distance\n\n  d(x,y) = arcosh( 1 + 2\u00b7||x-y||^2 / ( (1-||x||^2)(1-||y||^2) ) ).\n\nKarcherMean(S): the point m in B minimising sum_{y in S} d(m,y)^2, obtained by Riemannian gradient descent with step 1, initialised at the Euclidean mean of S projected by x -> x\u00b7(1-1e-6)/max(1,||x||), stopped at ||grad|| < 1e-8 or 30 iterations, whichever comes first (step 1 and the cap 30 are fixed a priori, not fitted).\nbeta = 1/tau_ref, where tau_ref is the contrastive temperature stored in the frozen Iss",
      "measured": false,
      "measurement": null,
      "family": "behaviour_contrast"
    },
    {
      "metric_id": "hgca_l1",
      "title": "Hyperbolic Gromov-ancestry AUC of the level-1 cell (two-tree agreement between the trie's branch and the reference's common-ancestor depth)",
      "round": "round_20261030_092444",
      "proposed_by": "metric_ideation_3",
      "formula": "Items i=1..N (N=24587), integer codes k_i=(k_i1,...,k_iL). Reference points x_s(i), x_t(i) in the Poincare ball B_c={p in R^d : c||p||^2<1} of curvature -c, with c=c_R (the curvature stored with the frozen reference artifact; no new constant).\n  d(u,v) = (1/sqrt(c)) * arcosh( 1 + 2c||u-v||^2 / ((1-c||u||^2)(1-c||v||^2)) ).\n  For every training interaction (u,i) used as a query: target i+=i, history H(u,i) = the training items of u strictly before i, truncated to the most recent 200 (compute cap, not tuned).\n  Query point q = Einstein midpoint of {x_s(j) : j in H}: k_j = 2x_s(j)/(1+c||x_s(j)||^",
      "measured": false,
      "measurement": null,
      "family": "behaviour_contrast"
    },
